{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00007",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.51,
      "end_seconds": 6.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Uh, hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.76,
      "end_seconds": 10.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.58,
      "end_seconds": 17.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Right, I've been dealing with cramping pain in the lower tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.91,
      "end_seconds": 21.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "When did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.84,
      "end_seconds": 25.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Probably three weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.58,
      "end_seconds": 36.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.7,
      "end_seconds": 46.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.27,
      "text": "Yeah, pretty severe, if I'm being honest. Certain foods and stress definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.99,
      "end_seconds": 51.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.31,
      "end_seconds": 57.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "It usually comes with a feeling of not emptying fully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.55,
      "end_seconds": 61.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.66,
      "end_seconds": 64.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.73,
      "end_seconds": 65.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.9,
      "end_seconds": 79.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "As for passing a lot of wind, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.88,
      "end_seconds": 86.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Have you had cramping pain in the lower tummy before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.26,
      "end_seconds": 94.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.07,
      "end_seconds": 99.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Can I take your vitals now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.54,
      "end_seconds": 111.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Rest your hand here..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.92,
      "end_seconds": 132.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 70, saturation 97 percent, temperature is 37.0 degrees, respiratory rate 14, pressure 127 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.42,
      "end_seconds": 136.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I mean, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.64,
      "end_seconds": 141.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "I'll explain what that means shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.92,
      "end_seconds": 146.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Okay, I need to examine you for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.42,
      "end_seconds": 150.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.25,
      "end_seconds": 162.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.62,
      "end_seconds": 178.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.76,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit up. Okay, have you had any blood in the stool, weight loss, family history of bowel cancer or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.33,
      "end_seconds": 181.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No. None of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.87,
      "end_seconds": 185.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.74,
      "end_seconds": 189.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.07,
      "end_seconds": 197.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.96,
      "end_seconds": 212.14,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.47,
      "end_seconds": 217.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.94,
      "end_seconds": 222.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "It's pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.91,
      "end_seconds": 241.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.27,
      "end_seconds": 259.46,
      "duration_seconds": 17.19,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago. I smoke, yes, around five a day. I share a flat with two friends. I eat out quite a lot, to be honest. Barely, I'm mostly sedentary these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.24,
      "end_seconds": 264.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Have you got any chronic problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.12,
      "end_seconds": 268.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.45,
      "end_seconds": 270.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm-hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.99,
      "end_seconds": 272.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I've got anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.47,
      "end_seconds": 278.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Okay, I can see anxiety in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.23,
      "end_seconds": 290.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Have you ever been under the knife?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.16,
      "end_seconds": 294.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Just a C-section, about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.77,
      "end_seconds": 305.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? It fits best with irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. I can't rule out coeliac disease yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.4,
      "end_seconds": 326.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Any scans or blood work done already?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.51,
      "end_seconds": 338.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "I had a coeliac test done at another clinic a few months ago. I don't have the report with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.03,
      "end_seconds": 344.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a stool calprotectin for bowel symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 345.6,
      "end_seconds": 350.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "We have a slot Friday at 10 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.14,
      "end_seconds": 359.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "We should do blood tests for bowel symptoms. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.37,
      "end_seconds": 362.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.35,
      "end_seconds": 384.93,
      "duration_seconds": 20.58,
      "text": "The treatment will be mebeverine, 135 milligrams, three times a day, for four weeks. You take it by mouth. That's for abdominal cramps. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. That's it on my side. Anything unclear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.93,
      "end_seconds": 388.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Thanks so much, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.05,
      "end_seconds": 390.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}